---
import { studio } from '../../data/studio.js';
import BoardUnit from './BoardUnit.astro';

const { yearsOnTools } = studio.founder;
const { email } = studio.contact;
const site = studio.proof.ownSite;
const host = site.url.replace('https://', '');
---
<!--
DIRECTION CONTRACT / candidate 02

THESIS: The board sells, not the copy. This page refuses the studio hero the
category always ships, a laptop mockup of a website on a dark gradient, and puts
the visitor's own working object on the screen instead, drawn correctly.

OWN-WORLD: Charcoal ground, one raised metal enclosure. Component language is DIN
rail hardware: butted modules with no gaps, a busbar, cover screws, flying neutral
tails, a schedule card. Clash Display for numbers and ratings, Satoshi for
everything else. The signature yellow into cyan gradient appears exactly once, as
the energised busbar, and nowhere else on the page.

STORY: A spark recognises the board in half a second, sees details only a trade
person would know to draw, and concludes this studio understands the job. Then he
mails enquiries@wyelectrical.co.uk.

FIRST VIEWPORT: Left column, roughly 38%, holds the h1 at clamp 34 to 56px, a 20
word lead, and two buttons, the yellow one first. Right column holds the board at
full column width, vertically centred, with a live status line beneath it.

FORM: Brief pinned, so no concept roll was run. Staging is the interactive
demonstration: the sequence plays once, then the board stays switchable.
-->
<section class="bhero shell">
  <div class="bhero__grid">

    <div class="bhero__say">
      <h1 class="bhero__h">{yearsOnTools} years on the tools. Now we build websites.</h1>

      <p class="bhero__lead">
        Websites for electricians and solar installers. Built by a spark, so
        you'll never have to explain what an EICR is.
      </p>

      <div class="bhero__do">
        <a class="btn btn--action" href={`mailto:${email}`}>Get in touch</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={site.url} rel="noopener">See {host}</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="bhero__board">
      <BoardUnit />
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
